{
  "statement": "I appreciate the ongoing discussions regarding energy reduction (GRN-07) and the need for performance efficiency. However, I must emphasize that safety and compliance must remain our top priorities. Therefore, I propose a synthesis that maintains strict documentation for any relaxation of jerk limits during emergencies (SAF-04) while ensuring that energy usage reductions during critical failures (GRN-07) do not compromise the system's adherence to safety and regulatory standards (RES-01, RES-02). This way, we can ensure that ethical and compliance standards are upheld while addressing efficiency and sustainability.",
